Netbeat: A tiny, automated network testing suite

DESCRIPTION
Netbeat is an automated network testing script that
runs a variety of networking tests to assess hardware,
host and service availability.

CONFIGURATION
Netbeat can be configured with its configuration file, named 'netbeat.conf'.
Here, you can alter the values of the fields to fit your needs:

1. router-ip: the IP address of your router. In most cases, this value should
be either 192.168.0.1 or 192.168.1.1. Verify your router's IP address
is correct before running Netbeat as virtually all tests will fail
in the absence of a reliable internet gateway.

2. dns-ip: the IP address of your DNS server In some instances, this may be the 
same IP address as your router because many routers also provide DNS services.
However, if you are using a public DNS server, such as the one provided by Cloudflare 
or Google, enter that IP address as the value for this variable.

3. test-website: the name of the website which will be used in an availability test involving
sending an HTTPS request to it. Do not include "http://" or "https://" in this variable's value
as it is not needed; only the name of the website without it. Including the HTTP or HTTPS
beginnings in the variable's name will cause name conflicts when trying to send an HTTPS request
to the website.

4. log-name: the name of the JSON file to write the results of the network test to.
Do not include the ".json" extension in the name of the variable's value as this will cause
the file name to have a double file extension.

5. timeout: the number of seconds to wait before giving up on a particular network test. 
A shorter timeout value is recommended for optimal performance and quicker assessment
of website availability.

GENERAL USE
In the directory you have downloaded Netbeat in, run the command: “python3 netbeat.py”. 
Ensure that netbeat.conf is in the same directory as the script is.
Netbeat will start the network health tests immediately and will display relevant 
output to the console regarding the status, completion, or failure of a particular
network health test. There are a total of 6 network health tests, with each varying
in specified tasks including testing hardware availability, network latency, and
download and upload speeds over the network. It is worth noting that Netbeat
will not perform a test DNS lookup in the event that the DNS server ping test failed.
Additionally, any errors that happen during the network health tests will appear on screen.
After all the tests have run, Netbeat will generate a JSON file containing a structured list
of the network health test performed and their resulting outcomes. Read this file
in order to understand the general health of your network and implement any networking 
solutions or troubleshoot any networking issues as needed.

